[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186188276 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-58e1bdfb-9550-5950-b391-e8892b95af10" "question-1e85b0be-111d-5b57-b950-c149f90f77dc"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188536 :question/problem "Given the joint probability distribution for two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ below, find $\\text{E}[Y].$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals.\n\n| $f(x,y)$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $…$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ | $…$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.3$ | $0.25$ | $0.45$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore, the probability mass function for  $Y$ is given by the following table:\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.3$ | $0.25$ | $0.45$ |\n\nFinally, the  expected value of $Y$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}\\,{f}_{Y}({y}_{i}) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.3+1\\cdot 0.25+2\\cdot 0.45 \\\\  & =0+0.25+0.9 \\\\  & =1.15.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186185496 :answer-field/correct 17592186185497 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188296 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-57c74959-06e0-5008-b9fc-e618f65747e4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188538 :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}y, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{3}{4},$ find $\\text{E}[4X+6Y].$" :question/worked-solution "We're given $\\text{E}[X].$ So, we first need to compute $\\text{E}[Y].$\n\nThe marginal density function for $Y$ when $0\\le y\\le 2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}y[{x}^{3}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}y({1}^{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the  expected value of $Y$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y}(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\cdot \\frac{y}{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[{y}^{3}]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(8-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[4X+6Y] & =4\\,\\text{E}[X]+6\\,\\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =4(\\frac{3}{4})+6(\\frac{4}{3}) \\\\  & =3+8 \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186185508 :answer-field/correct 17592186185511 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-57c74959-06e0-5008-b9fc-e618f65747e4" :question/id #uuid "57c74959-06e0-5008-b9fc-e618f65747e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-143584" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{9}({x}^{3}+{y}^{3}), & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{23}{15},$ find $\\text{E}[3X-Y].$" :question/worked-solution "We're given $\\text{E}[Y].$ So, we first need to compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\nThe marginal density function for $X$ when $0\\le x\\le 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{2}{9}({x}^{3}+{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}{[{x}^{3}y+\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}(2{x}^{3}+\\frac{{2}^{4}}{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}({x}^{3}+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the  expected value of $X$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,{f}_{X}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot \\frac{4}{9}({x}^{3}+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{4}+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}{[\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}+{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}(\\frac{1}{5}+1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[3X-Y] & =3\\,\\text{E}[X]+(-1)\\,\\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =3\\,(\\frac{8}{15})-(\\frac{23}{15}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b3819eb9-9cd0-5d3c-852e-6d38178d3c62"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b3819eb9-9cd0-5d3c-852e-6d38178d3c62" :answer-field/id #uuid "b3819eb9-9cd0-5d3c-852e-6d38178d3c62" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bd2ebd72-45b1-5c05-82b9-a266f54fe224" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bd2ebd72-45b1-5c05-82b9-a266f54fe224" "answer-d551241c-84d6-5150-94ac-c0e6751dcdf3" "answer-9cdb3a18-70b7-5be8-85e6-7d754574d6e7" "answer-320777af-ae37-523c-bacf-e28e66480cc3" "answer-7852e317-6684-5e8f-b211-c3d2fd1b2920"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd2ebd72-45b1-5c05-82b9-a266f54fe224" :answer/id #uuid "bd2ebd72-45b1-5c05-82b9-a266f54fe224" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d551241c-84d6-5150-94ac-c0e6751dcdf3" :answer/id #uuid "d551241c-84d6-5150-94ac-c0e6751dcdf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9cdb3a18-70b7-5be8-85e6-7d754574d6e7" :answer/id #uuid "9cdb3a18-70b7-5be8-85e6-7d754574d6e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-320777af-ae37-523c-bacf-e28e66480cc3" :answer/id #uuid "320777af-ae37-523c-bacf-e28e66480cc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7852e317-6684-5e8f-b211-c3d2fd1b2920" :answer/id #uuid "7852e317-6684-5e8f-b211-c3d2fd1b2920" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-58e1bdfb-9550-5950-b391-e8892b95af10" :question/id #uuid "58e1bdfb-9550-5950-b391-e8892b95af10" :question/math-academy-id "q-143604" :question/problem "Given the joint probability distribution for two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ below, find $\\text{E}[2X+4Y].$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=-2$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=-1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=-2$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=-1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ | $0.35$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.35$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.2$ | $0.2$ | $0.35$ | $0.25$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore,  the probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y$ are given by the following tables:\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{X}(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.35$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.35$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"50\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{Y}(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.35$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nNow, we can compute the expected values for $X$ and $Y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}\\,{f}_{X}({x}_{i}) \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 0.3+1\\cdot 0.35+3\\cdot 0.35 \\\\  & =-0.3+0.35+1.05 \\\\  & =1.1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}\\,{f}_{Y}({y}_{i}) \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot 0.2+0\\cdot 0.2+2\\cdot 0.35+4\\cdot 0.25 \\\\  & =-0.4+0+0.7+1 \\\\  & =1.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the properties of expectation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[2X+4Y] & =2\\text{E}[X]+4\\,\\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =2(1.1)+4(1.3) \\\\  & =2.2+5.2 \\\\  & =7.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5c3d7ec3-2b65-5d8c-8b98-80722d885c87"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5c3d7ec3-2b65-5d8c-8b98-80722d885c87" :answer-field/id #uuid "5c3d7ec3-2b65-5d8c-8b98-80722d885c87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-221fa59d-39a2-5c91-a249-8862c6b794b6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a166d431-6741-566e-a4d1-3e91ef5f0388" "answer-a02fd45f-1410-54c4-bb64-034b16bd73d1" "answer-221fa59d-39a2-5c91-a249-8862c6b794b6" "answer-82e3153b-16a6-58ac-b3a6-8a86fae4ce60" "answer-3e0b2a8d-ea50-5575-ae8b-df8e61b4fd0a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a166d431-6741-566e-a4d1-3e91ef5f0388" :answer/id #uuid "a166d431-6741-566e-a4d1-3e91ef5f0388" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a02fd45f-1410-54c4-bb64-034b16bd73d1" :answer/id #uuid "a02fd45f-1410-54c4-bb64-034b16bd73d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-221fa59d-39a2-5c91-a249-8862c6b794b6" :answer/id #uuid "221fa59d-39a2-5c91-a249-8862c6b794b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82e3153b-16a6-58ac-b3a6-8a86fae4ce60" :answer/id #uuid "82e3153b-16a6-58ac-b3a6-8a86fae4ce60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9.05" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e0b2a8d-ea50-5575-ae8b-df8e61b4fd0a" :answer/id #uuid "3e0b2a8d-ea50-5575-ae8b-df8e61b4fd0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1e85b0be-111d-5b57-b950-c149f90f77dc" :question/id #uuid "1e85b0be-111d-5b57-b950-c149f90f77dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-149599" :question/problem "Given the joint probability distribution for two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ below, find $\\text{E}[Y].$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=-2$ | $Y=-1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals.\n\n| $f(x,y)$ | $Y=-2$ | $Y=-1$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ | $…$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ | $…$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $…$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore, the probability mass function for  $Y$ is given by the following table:\n\n| $y$ | $-2$ | $-1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ |\n\nFinally, the  expected value of $Y$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}\\,{f}_{Y}({y}_{i}) \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot 0.4+(-1)\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =-0.8-0.6 \\\\  & =-1.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c8ce17d4-130c-5b9e-a7e1-458cb727bad8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c8ce17d4-130c-5b9e-a7e1-458cb727bad8" :answer-field/id #uuid "c8ce17d4-130c-5b9e-a7e1-458cb727bad8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-54921f49-41bd-59ea-87fa-1aa8a31bf9f6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c6bc73a6-19e3-5079-8075-c87f32448b75" "answer-54921f49-41bd-59ea-87fa-1aa8a31bf9f6" "answer-8af359a3-0397-596f-9263-82e98df0c5e7" "answer-e6ed4ece-6571-5aa6-a239-9c83bba0bbb7" "answer-b6ef201f-91de-5739-8423-ca5f69f9f69b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6bc73a6-19e3-5079-8075-c87f32448b75" :answer/id #uuid "c6bc73a6-19e3-5079-8075-c87f32448b75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-54921f49-41bd-59ea-87fa-1aa8a31bf9f6" :answer/id #uuid "54921f49-41bd-59ea-87fa-1aa8a31bf9f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8af359a3-0397-596f-9263-82e98df0c5e7" :answer/id #uuid "8af359a3-0397-596f-9263-82e98df0c5e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e6ed4ece-6571-5aa6-a239-9c83bba0bbb7" :answer/id #uuid "e6ed4ece-6571-5aa6-a239-9c83bba0bbb7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b6ef201f-91de-5739-8423-ca5f69f9f69b" :answer/id #uuid "b6ef201f-91de-5739-8423-ca5f69f9f69b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-827978e3-994c-5c29-a170-80728a4bfa3b" :activity/id #uuid "827978e3-994c-5c29-a170-80728a4bfa3b" :activity/title "Computing Expected Values From Joint Distributions" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048466 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-b0485605-8f6d-579c-978c-558250074dc2" "step-0dca7aaf-6bc5-5c2a-8c78-4a283b1cbdad" "step-6611e889-3327-54b2-b32f-c65fbae23e9b" "step-febeff6c-5ada-57a3-a1f8-8bc1079ec0d0" "step-e610be17-d713-5476-8573-4ab202853156"] :activity/first-step "step-b0485605-8f6d-579c-978c-558250074dc2" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-b0485605-8f6d-579c-978c-558250074dc2" :step/id #uuid "b0485605-8f6d-579c-978c-558250074dc2" :step/content 17592186188536 :step/next "step-0dca7aaf-6bc5-5c2a-8c78-4a283b1cbdad" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-0dca7aaf-6bc5-5c2a-8c78-4a283b1cbdad" :step/id #uuid "0dca7aaf-6bc5-5c2a-8c78-4a283b1cbdad" :step/content 17592186188538 :step/next "step-6611e889-3327-54b2-b32f-c65fbae23e9b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-6611e889-3327-54b2-b32f-c65fbae23e9b" :step/id #uuid "6611e889-3327-54b2-b32f-c65fbae23e9b" :step/content "question-57c74959-06e0-5008-b9fc-e618f65747e4" :step/next "step-febeff6c-5ada-57a3-a1f8-8bc1079ec0d0" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-febeff6c-5ada-57a3-a1f8-8bc1079ec0d0" :step/id #uuid "febeff6c-5ada-57a3-a1f8-8bc1079ec0d0" :step/content "question-58e1bdfb-9550-5950-b391-e8892b95af10" :step/next "step-e610be17-d713-5476-8573-4ab202853156" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-e610be17-d713-5476-8573-4ab202853156" :step/id #uuid "e610be17-d713-5476-8573-4ab202853156" :step/content "question-1e85b0be-111d-5b57-b950-c149f90f77dc" :db/ensure [:step/validate]}] "assertions" [[17592186188536 :question/problem "Given the joint probability distribution for two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ below, find $\\text{E}[Y].$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ |"] [17592186188536 :question/worked-solution "Recall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals.\n\n| $f(x,y)$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $…$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ | $…$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.3$ | $0.25$ | $0.45$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore, the probability mass function for  $Y$ is given by the following table:\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.3$ | $0.25$ | $0.45$ |\n\nFinally, the  expected value of $Y$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}\\,{f}_{Y}({y}_{i}) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.3+1\\cdot 0.25+2\\cdot 0.45 \\\\  & =0+0.25+0.9 \\\\  & =1.15.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186188536 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [17592186185496 :answer-field/correct 17592186185497] [17592186188538 :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}y, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{3}{4},$ find $\\text{E}[4X+6Y].$"] [17592186188538 :question/worked-solution "We're given $\\text{E}[X].$ So, we first need to compute $\\text{E}[Y].$\n\nThe marginal density function for $Y$ when $0\\le y\\le 2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}y[{x}^{3}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}y({1}^{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the  expected value of $Y$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y}(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\cdot \\frac{y}{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[{y}^{3}]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(8-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[4X+6Y] & =4\\,\\text{E}[X]+6\\,\\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =4(\\frac{3}{4})+6(\\frac{4}{3}) \\\\  & =3+8 \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186188538 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [17592186185508 :answer-field/correct 17592186185511] ["question-57c74959-06e0-5008-b9fc-e618f65747e4" :question/id #uuid "57c74959-06e0-5008-b9fc-e618f65747e4"] ["question-57c74959-06e0-5008-b9fc-e618f65747e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-143584"] ["question-57c74959-06e0-5008-b9fc-e618f65747e4" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{9}({x}^{3}+{y}^{3}), & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{23}{15},$ find $\\text{E}[3X-Y].$"] ["question-57c74959-06e0-5008-b9fc-e618f65747e4" :question/worked-solution "We're given $\\text{E}[Y].$ So, we first need to compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\nThe marginal density function for $X$ when $0\\le x\\le 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{2}{9}({x}^{3}+{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}{[{x}^{3}y+\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}(2{x}^{3}+\\frac{{2}^{4}}{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}({x}^{3}+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the  expected value of $X$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,{f}_{X}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot \\frac{4}{9}({x}^{3}+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{4}+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}{[\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}+{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}(\\frac{1}{5}+1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[3X-Y] & =3\\,\\text{E}[X]+(-1)\\,\\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =3\\,(\\frac{8}{15})-(\\frac{23}{15}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-57c74959-06e0-5008-b9fc-e618f65747e4" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-b3819eb9-9cd0-5d3c-852e-6d38178d3c62" :answer-field/id #uuid "b3819eb9-9cd0-5d3c-852e-6d38178d3c62"] ["answer-bd2ebd72-45b1-5c05-82b9-a266f54fe224" :answer/id #uuid "bd2ebd72-45b1-5c05-82b9-a266f54fe224"] ["answer-bd2ebd72-45b1-5c05-82b9-a266f54fe224" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-bd2ebd72-45b1-5c05-82b9-a266f54fe224" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{15}"] ["answer-d551241c-84d6-5150-94ac-c0e6751dcdf3" :answer/id #uuid "d551241c-84d6-5150-94ac-c0e6751dcdf3"] ["answer-d551241c-84d6-5150-94ac-c0e6751dcdf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d551241c-84d6-5150-94ac-c0e6751dcdf3" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["answer-9cdb3a18-70b7-5be8-85e6-7d754574d6e7" :answer/id #uuid "9cdb3a18-70b7-5be8-85e6-7d754574d6e7"] ["answer-9cdb3a18-70b7-5be8-85e6-7d754574d6e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9cdb3a18-70b7-5be8-85e6-7d754574d6e7" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}"] ["answer-320777af-ae37-523c-bacf-e28e66480cc3" :answer/id #uuid "320777af-ae37-523c-bacf-e28e66480cc3"] ["answer-320777af-ae37-523c-bacf-e28e66480cc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-320777af-ae37-523c-bacf-e28e66480cc3" :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}"] ["answer-7852e317-6684-5e8f-b211-c3d2fd1b2920" :answer/id #uuid "7852e317-6684-5e8f-b211-c3d2fd1b2920"] ["answer-7852e317-6684-5e8f-b211-c3d2fd1b2920" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7852e317-6684-5e8f-b211-c3d2fd1b2920" :answer/value "\\frac{4}{15}"] ["answer-field-b3819eb9-9cd0-5d3c-852e-6d38178d3c62" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-b3819eb9-9cd0-5d3c-852e-6d38178d3c62" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-b3819eb9-9cd0-5d3c-852e-6d38178d3c62" :answer-field/correct "answer-bd2ebd72-45b1-5c05-82b9-a266f54fe224"] ["answer-field-b3819eb9-9cd0-5d3c-852e-6d38178d3c62" :answer-field/choices "answer-bd2ebd72-45b1-5c05-82b9-a266f54fe224"] ["answer-field-b3819eb9-9cd0-5d3c-852e-6d38178d3c62" :answer-field/choices "answer-d551241c-84d6-5150-94ac-c0e6751dcdf3"] ["answer-field-b3819eb9-9cd0-5d3c-852e-6d38178d3c62" :answer-field/choices "answer-9cdb3a18-70b7-5be8-85e6-7d754574d6e7"] ["answer-field-b3819eb9-9cd0-5d3c-852e-6d38178d3c62" :answer-field/choices "answer-320777af-ae37-523c-bacf-e28e66480cc3"] ["answer-field-b3819eb9-9cd0-5d3c-852e-6d38178d3c62" :answer-field/choices "answer-7852e317-6684-5e8f-b211-c3d2fd1b2920"] ["question-57c74959-06e0-5008-b9fc-e618f65747e4" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-b3819eb9-9cd0-5d3c-852e-6d38178d3c62"] [17592186188296 :knowledge-point/questions "question-57c74959-06e0-5008-b9fc-e618f65747e4"] ["question-58e1bdfb-9550-5950-b391-e8892b95af10" :question/id #uuid "58e1bdfb-9550-5950-b391-e8892b95af10"] ["question-58e1bdfb-9550-5950-b391-e8892b95af10" :question/math-academy-id "q-143604"] ["question-58e1bdfb-9550-5950-b391-e8892b95af10" :question/problem "Given the joint probability distribution for two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ below, find $\\text{E}[2X+4Y].$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=-2$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=-1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ |"] ["question-58e1bdfb-9550-5950-b391-e8892b95af10" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=-2$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=-1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ | $0.35$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.35$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.2$ | $0.2$ | $0.35$ | $0.25$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore,  the probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y$ are given by the following tables:\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{X}(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.35$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.35$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"50\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{Y}(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.35$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nNow, we can compute the expected values for $X$ and $Y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}\\,{f}_{X}({x}_{i}) \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 0.3+1\\cdot 0.35+3\\cdot 0.35 \\\\  & =-0.3+0.35+1.05 \\\\  & =1.1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}\\,{f}_{Y}({y}_{i}) \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot 0.2+0\\cdot 0.2+2\\cdot 0.35+4\\cdot 0.25 \\\\  & =-0.4+0+0.7+1 \\\\  & =1.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the properties of expectation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[2X+4Y] & =2\\text{E}[X]+4\\,\\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =2(1.1)+4(1.3) \\\\  & =2.2+5.2 \\\\  & =7.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-58e1bdfb-9550-5950-b391-e8892b95af10" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-5c3d7ec3-2b65-5d8c-8b98-80722d885c87" :answer-field/id #uuid "5c3d7ec3-2b65-5d8c-8b98-80722d885c87"] ["answer-a166d431-6741-566e-a4d1-3e91ef5f0388" :answer/id #uuid "a166d431-6741-566e-a4d1-3e91ef5f0388"] ["answer-a166d431-6741-566e-a4d1-3e91ef5f0388" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a166d431-6741-566e-a4d1-3e91ef5f0388" :answer/value "5.9"] ["answer-a02fd45f-1410-54c4-bb64-034b16bd73d1" :answer/id #uuid "a02fd45f-1410-54c4-bb64-034b16bd73d1"] ["answer-a02fd45f-1410-54c4-bb64-034b16bd73d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a02fd45f-1410-54c4-bb64-034b16bd73d1" :answer/value "6.5"] ["answer-221fa59d-39a2-5c91-a249-8862c6b794b6" :answer/id #uuid "221fa59d-39a2-5c91-a249-8862c6b794b6"] ["answer-221fa59d-39a2-5c91-a249-8862c6b794b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-221fa59d-39a2-5c91-a249-8862c6b794b6" :answer/value "7.4"] ["answer-82e3153b-16a6-58ac-b3a6-8a86fae4ce60" :answer/id #uuid "82e3153b-16a6-58ac-b3a6-8a86fae4ce60"] ["answer-82e3153b-16a6-58ac-b3a6-8a86fae4ce60" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-82e3153b-16a6-58ac-b3a6-8a86fae4ce60" :answer/value "9.05"] ["answer-3e0b2a8d-ea50-5575-ae8b-df8e61b4fd0a" :answer/id #uuid "3e0b2a8d-ea50-5575-ae8b-df8e61b4fd0a"] ["answer-3e0b2a8d-ea50-5575-ae8b-df8e61b4fd0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-3e0b2a8d-ea50-5575-ae8b-df8e61b4fd0a" :answer/value "9.2"] ["answer-field-5c3d7ec3-2b65-5d8c-8b98-80722d885c87" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-5c3d7ec3-2b65-5d8c-8b98-80722d885c87" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-5c3d7ec3-2b65-5d8c-8b98-80722d885c87" :answer-field/correct "answer-221fa59d-39a2-5c91-a249-8862c6b794b6"] ["answer-field-5c3d7ec3-2b65-5d8c-8b98-80722d885c87" :answer-field/choices "answer-a166d431-6741-566e-a4d1-3e91ef5f0388"] ["answer-field-5c3d7ec3-2b65-5d8c-8b98-80722d885c87" :answer-field/choices "answer-a02fd45f-1410-54c4-bb64-034b16bd73d1"] ["answer-field-5c3d7ec3-2b65-5d8c-8b98-80722d885c87" :answer-field/choices "answer-221fa59d-39a2-5c91-a249-8862c6b794b6"] ["answer-field-5c3d7ec3-2b65-5d8c-8b98-80722d885c87" :answer-field/choices "answer-82e3153b-16a6-58ac-b3a6-8a86fae4ce60"] ["answer-field-5c3d7ec3-2b65-5d8c-8b98-80722d885c87" :answer-field/choices "answer-3e0b2a8d-ea50-5575-ae8b-df8e61b4fd0a"] ["question-58e1bdfb-9550-5950-b391-e8892b95af10" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-5c3d7ec3-2b65-5d8c-8b98-80722d885c87"] [17592186188276 :knowledge-point/questions "question-58e1bdfb-9550-5950-b391-e8892b95af10"] ["question-1e85b0be-111d-5b57-b950-c149f90f77dc" :question/id #uuid "1e85b0be-111d-5b57-b950-c149f90f77dc"] ["question-1e85b0be-111d-5b57-b950-c149f90f77dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-149599"] ["question-1e85b0be-111d-5b57-b950-c149f90f77dc" :question/problem "Given the joint probability distribution for two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ below, find $\\text{E}[Y].$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=-2$ | $Y=-1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ |"] ["question-1e85b0be-111d-5b57-b950-c149f90f77dc" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals.\n\n| $f(x,y)$ | $Y=-2$ | $Y=-1$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ | $…$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ | $…$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $…$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore, the probability mass function for  $Y$ is given by the following table:\n\n| $y$ | $-2$ | $-1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ |\n\nFinally, the  expected value of $Y$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}\\,{f}_{Y}({y}_{i}) \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot 0.4+(-1)\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =-0.8-0.6 \\\\  & =-1.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-1e85b0be-111d-5b57-b950-c149f90f77dc" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-c8ce17d4-130c-5b9e-a7e1-458cb727bad8" :answer-field/id #uuid "c8ce17d4-130c-5b9e-a7e1-458cb727bad8"] ["answer-c6bc73a6-19e3-5079-8075-c87f32448b75" :answer/id #uuid "c6bc73a6-19e3-5079-8075-c87f32448b75"] ["answer-c6bc73a6-19e3-5079-8075-c87f32448b75" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c6bc73a6-19e3-5079-8075-c87f32448b75" :answer/value "-1.2"] ["answer-54921f49-41bd-59ea-87fa-1aa8a31bf9f6" :answer/id #uuid "54921f49-41bd-59ea-87fa-1aa8a31bf9f6"] ["answer-54921f49-41bd-59ea-87fa-1aa8a31bf9f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-54921f49-41bd-59ea-87fa-1aa8a31bf9f6" :answer/value "-1.4"] ["answer-8af359a3-0397-596f-9263-82e98df0c5e7" :answer/id #uuid "8af359a3-0397-596f-9263-82e98df0c5e7"] ["answer-8af359a3-0397-596f-9263-82e98df0c5e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8af359a3-0397-596f-9263-82e98df0c5e7" :answer/value "-1.5"] ["answer-e6ed4ece-6571-5aa6-a239-9c83bba0bbb7" :answer/id #uuid "e6ed4ece-6571-5aa6-a239-9c83bba0bbb7"] ["answer-e6ed4ece-6571-5aa6-a239-9c83bba0bbb7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e6ed4ece-6571-5aa6-a239-9c83bba0bbb7" :answer/value "-1.6"] ["answer-b6ef201f-91de-5739-8423-ca5f69f9f69b" :answer/id #uuid "b6ef201f-91de-5739-8423-ca5f69f9f69b"] ["answer-b6ef201f-91de-5739-8423-ca5f69f9f69b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b6ef201f-91de-5739-8423-ca5f69f9f69b" :answer/value "-1.8"] ["answer-field-c8ce17d4-130c-5b9e-a7e1-458cb727bad8" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-c8ce17d4-130c-5b9e-a7e1-458cb727bad8" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-c8ce17d4-130c-5b9e-a7e1-458cb727bad8" :answer-field/correct "answer-54921f49-41bd-59ea-87fa-1aa8a31bf9f6"] ["answer-field-c8ce17d4-130c-5b9e-a7e1-458cb727bad8" :answer-field/choices "answer-c6bc73a6-19e3-5079-8075-c87f32448b75"] ["answer-field-c8ce17d4-130c-5b9e-a7e1-458cb727bad8" :answer-field/choices "answer-54921f49-41bd-59ea-87fa-1aa8a31bf9f6"] ["answer-field-c8ce17d4-130c-5b9e-a7e1-458cb727bad8" :answer-field/choices "answer-8af359a3-0397-596f-9263-82e98df0c5e7"] ["answer-field-c8ce17d4-130c-5b9e-a7e1-458cb727bad8" :answer-field/choices "answer-e6ed4ece-6571-5aa6-a239-9c83bba0bbb7"] ["answer-field-c8ce17d4-130c-5b9e-a7e1-458cb727bad8" :answer-field/choices "answer-b6ef201f-91de-5739-8423-ca5f69f9f69b"] ["question-1e85b0be-111d-5b57-b950-c149f90f77dc" :ques